.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.19757889075596813,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":1.5824175824175823,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.02178,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":14.5,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Aclaris Therapeutics, Inc., a clinical-stage biopharmaceutical company, engages in the discovering and developing novel molecule product candidates for immuno-inflammatory diseases in the United States. The company product pipeline includes Bosakitug (ATI-045), an anti-thymic stromal lymphopoietin monoclonal antibody in Phase 2 trial to treat moderate to severe atopic dermatitis, asthma, chronic rhinosinusitis with nasal polyps, and moderate to severe chronic obstructive pulmonary disease; ATI-2138, an potent and selective novel investigational dual inhibitor of ITK and JAK3 in Phase 2a trial for the treatment for T cell-mediated autoimmune diseases; ATI-052, a humanized anti-TSLP and anti-IL4R bispecific antibody in Phase 1b to treat various atopic, immunologic, and respiratory diseases; ATI-9494, an oral, covalent, investigational dual inhibitor of ITK and Resting Lymphocyte Kinase (TXK), and other covalent JAK-sparing ITK inhibitors to treat modulate T cell biology across various diseases; and Lepzacitinib, a soft JAK 1/3 inhibitor for the treatment of atopic dermatitis and other dermatologic conditions. Aclaris Therapeutics, Inc. was incorporated in 2012 and is headquartered in Wayne, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Neal S. Walker D.O., M.D. | Co-Founder, CEO & Chairman | Age 55 | Compensation: $965,550 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 69 people. Revenue per employee of $113K ranks in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers, improving at 21%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $179K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 9\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Aclaris Therapeutics, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $604M market cap on $8M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -36% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -430% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 30%.","The company is burning through $47M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at -11.1% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 158% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 2.2% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-3.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Healthcare peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 976% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.6% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Healthcare peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 134% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Aclaris Therapeutics (ACRS) Reports Q3 Loss, Beats Revenue Estimates","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3024216/aclaris-therapeutics-acrs-reports-q3-loss-beats-revenue-estimates?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_4-3024216","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793885709.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.318,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Aclaris Therapeutics, Inc. $ACRS Position Boosted by Profund Advisors LLC","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/04/aclaris-therapeutics-inc-acrs-position-boosted-by-profund-advisors-llc.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793787908.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.886,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Aclaris Therapeutics (NASDAQ:ACRS) & Oncocyte (NASDAQ:IMDX) Head-To-Head Review","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnia